  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c **** /**
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @brief Q15 Complex matrix multiplication
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcA points to the first input complex matrix structure
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcB points to the second input complex matrix structure
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @param[out]      *pDst points to output complex matrix structure
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @param[in]		*pScratch points to the array for storing intermediate results
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @return     		The function returns either
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * <code>ARM_MATH_SIZE_MISMATCH</code> or <code>ARM_MATH_SUCCESS</code> based on the outcome of siz
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * \par Conditions for optimum performance
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *  Input, output and state buffers should be aligned by 32-bit
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * \par Restrictions
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *  If the silicon does not support unaligned memory access enable the macro UNALIGNED_SUPPORT_DISA
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *	In this case input, output, scratch buffers should be aligned by 32-bit
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * @details
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * \par
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 64-bit internal accumulator. The inputs to the
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * multiplications are in 1.15 format and multiplications yield a 2.30 result.
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * The 2.30 intermediate
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * results are accumulated in a 64-bit accumulator in 34.30 format. This approach
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * provides 33 guard bits and there is no risk of overflow. The 34.30 result is then
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * truncated to 34.15 format by discarding the low 15 bits and then saturated to
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * 1.15 format.
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * \par
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  * Refer to <code>arm_mat_mult_fast_q15()</code> for a faster but less precise version of this func
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  *
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_q15.c ****  */
